{
  "_comment": [
    "P5-T05 (#62) conformance set: 50 valid mappings plus adversarial cases.",
    "",
    "This is TEST DATA, not Odoo data — it is read by tests/test_domain_mapper.py",
    "by path and is deliberately NOT listed in __manifest__.py, matching the",
    "convention already set by data/sample_questions.json.",
    "",
    "Each case is self-contained and deterministic:",
    "  model             - the whitelisted model the question is asked against",
    "  question          - what a user would type",
    "  provider_response - the EXACT string the LLM is made to return; the",
    "                      gateway is patched, so no provider is ever contacted",
    "  expected_domain   - what validate() must return (valid cases only)",
    "  expect            - 'refusal' for every case that must NOT produce a domain",
    "",
    "The provider responses are fixtures, not predictions: the point of a case is",
    "what the VALIDATOR does with a payload, so each one states the payload",
    "explicitly rather than hoping a model would produce it.",
    "",
    "Note V-cases use sale.order state 'sale' and never 'done' — Odoo 19 removed",
    "that value (see A15, which pins the refusal)."
  ],

  "cases": [
